  "outcome": {
    "final_answer": "Final Answer:\n- Report: `project/outputs/reports/task_report.md`\n- Key Results:\n  - The bulk RNA-seq data are most consistent with the PBMC cell type labeled **`CD4 TCM`** in the SingleCellExperiment reference.\n  - This label (`CD4 TCM`) has the highest aggregated Pearson similarity (`pearson_mean ≈ 0.878685`) to the two bulk samples, slightly exceeding the next-best match (`Treg`, `pearson_mean ≈ 0.875776`).\n- Artifacts:\n  - Prediction summary (narrative): `project/outputs/reports/prediction_summary.md`\n  - Detailed report: `project/outputs/reports/task_report.md`\n  - Bulk QC summary: `project/outputs/tables/bulk_counts_summary.tsv`\n  - Gene intersection (shared Ensembl IDs): `project/outputs/tables/gene_intersection.tsv`\n  - Cell-type pseudobulk signatures (log1p-CPM): `project/outputs/tables/celltype_pseudobulk_signatures.tsv`\n  - Bulk vs cell-type similarity scores: `project/outputs/tables/bulk_vs_celltype_similarity.tsv`\n  - Final prediction table: `project/outputs/tables/predicted_celltype.tsv`\n  - Reference cell-type counts (header-only placeholder): `project/outputs/tables/reference_celltype_counts.tsv`\n- Caveats & Warnings:\n  - The margin between the top match (CD4 TCM) and the second-best (Treg) is small (`≈ 0.0029` in mean Pearson correlation), so although CD4 TCM is the best-supported single label, the bulk profile is also highly similar to Treg and may reflect closely related or mixed CD4 T-cell states.\n- Next Steps:\n  - Use marker genes distinguishing CD4 central memory T cells from Tregs to further validate the assignment if you examine the data directly.\n  - Inspect `bulk_vs_celltype_similarity.tsv` for the full ranking of cell types if you want to understand alternative plausible origins.",
